      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't want coping strategies. i've already tried \"processing\" this. i've tried to accept it. but how do you accept being a ghost in your own body? it feels so much more dignified to go out on my own terms while i can still recognize my reflection, instead of waiting until i'm just a patient in a gown who doesn't even know their own name. it feels like the only way to truly preserve myself is to not be here when the light finally goes out. doesn't that make sense?",
